# Server Backend — Best Practices

## Architecture

```
routes/ → controllers/ → models/
         ↓
    validators/ (input checks)
    middleware/ (auth, upload, rate limit)
    helpers/    (asyncHandler, response formatters)
    constants/  (messages, status codes)
```

No services layer unless a refactor is explicitly requested.

## Controllers

- Wrap every async handler with `asyncHandler` from `server/src/helpers/asyncHandler.js`
- Use `sendSuccess` / `sendError` / `sendData` from `server/src/helpers/response.js`
- Use `SUCCESS_MESSAGES` / `ERROR_MESSAGES` / `HTTP_STATUS` from `server/src/constants/messages.js`
- Keep controllers thin: validate → call model → format response

## Validation

- Input checks belong in `server/src/validators/`, not duplicated in controllers
- Wrap `JSON.parse(req.body.blog)` in try/catch for multipart blog creation

## Routes

- Static paths (`/all`) before param routes (`/:blogId`)
- Public routes before `router.use(auth)`
- Mutations use POST — do not switch to REST verbs without updating the client

## Middleware Stack (preserve order in `server.js`)

CORS → Helmet → body parser → rate limit → static uploads → logging → routes → 404 → error handler

## File Uploads

Use existing Multer config; store images in `uploads/blogs/`, serve via static middleware.

## Logging

Use `httpLogger` for requests/responses and `dbLogger` for database operations — follow existing emoji/format patterns.

## Do Not

- Return inconsistent JSON shapes — always include `success: boolean`
- Rename env vars without updating `.env.example`, `docker-compose.yml`, and `init-scripts/` together
- Add one-off helper files for logic used in a single place — keep it inline or in existing modules
- Skip error handling on model operations (check `findById` results before updating/deleting)
